    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Dedicatio.</l>
    <l n="2">ximè &amp; actu; sed remotè, &amp; quasi</l>
    <l n="3">potentiâ, factâ accuratiori ad sin-</l>
    <l n="4">gula attentione in actum deducen-</l>
    <l n="5">dâ: Adeòque prout semen virtute</l>
    <l n="6">est tota arbor, ita hæc scientia,</l>
    <l n="7">tota Philosophia, omnisque studio</l>
    <l n="8">humano acquisita notitia. Quare &amp; <i>γνωκωτάτη,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>καθολικὴ, imò &amp; καλ' ἐξοχὴν</i> Philosophia &amp; sapientia</l>
    <l n="10">merito audit. Hujus igitur Institu-</l>
    <l n="11">tiones tradere, apprimè necessari-</l>
    <l n="12">um videbitur; Prout hujus studi-</l>
    <l n="13">um maximè est utile; Quamob-</l>
    <l n="14">rem eas breviter adornare, inque</l>
    <l n="15">Discipulorū usum convertere con-</l>
    <l n="16">stitui; idque non tantum viva voce,</l>
    <l n="17">sed &amp; hacce <i>Ἀφορισμοί</i>, pro ra-</l>
    <l n="18">tione gratiæ Divinæ, præstare ten-</l>
    <l n="19">tavi: Quam dum publicæ luci,</l>
    <l n="20">publicis in Academiâ vestrâ Di-</l>
    <l n="21">sputationibus, in commodum Stu-</l>
    <l n="22">diosorum, qui meis curis se com-</l>
    <l n="23">mittunt, expono, non potui huncce</l>
    <l n="24">fru-</l>
